    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13098" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀπόλλων</span></b> , ὁ,
			<u>Apollo</u>: gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωνος</span> (also
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ω</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>An.Ox.</u>
			3.222
		</span></i>): acc. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀπόλλω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					1.9
				</span></i>
			, al., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				214
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1091
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tr.</u>
				209
			</span></i> (lyr.) (mostly in adjurations, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νὴτὸν
				Ἀπόλλω,</span> etc.), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀπόλλωνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					624a
				</span></i>
			, freq. later, <i><span class="en">
				Agatharch.
				7
			</span></i>, etc.: voc. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄπολλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alc.
					1
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				159
			</span></i>(lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				186
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀπόλλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					559
				</span></i>
			; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀπέλλων, Ἄπλουν.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pythag.
			</span></i> name of a number, <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Abst.</u>
				2.36
			</span></i>.</div>
